IDO (not shipped)
-----------------
  SGI's IDO 5.3 and 7.1 C compilers, which many N64 decompilation projects
  build with, are proprietary. romdev does not ship them, and no romdev npm
  package contains them. romdev-toolchain-ido is a private package in the
  source repository that npm will not publish. To use IDO, build it yourself
  from a checkout with packages/romdevtools/scripts/build-ido.sh (it
  statically recompiles the IRIX programs with the pinned ido-static-recomp,
  https://github.com/decompals/ido-static-recomp, MIT, and compiles the
  result to WebAssembly), or set ROMDEV_IDO_DIR to a directory holding your
  own build (its 5.3/ and 7.1/ folders). The IRIX programs remain the
  property of their owners.


